      "text": "The volume of a pyramid can be calculated using the formula $\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height}$.\n\nFor the original pyramid with a base edge of 12 cm, the base area is $12^2 = 144$ square centimeters. The original pyramid's height is 8 cm, so its volume is $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = 384$ cubic centimeters.\n\nFor the smaller pyramid cut from the original pyramid, with a base edge of 6 cm, the base area is $6^2 = 36$ square centimeters. The smaller pyramid's height is 4 cm, so its volume is $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = 48$ cubic centimeters.\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid. Therefore, the volume of the frustum is $384 - 48 = \\boxed{336}$ cubic centimeters.",
