      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we first need to calculate the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid. The volume \\( V \\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the volume of the original pyramid:\nThe base edge of the original pyramid is 12 cm, and its height is 8 cm. The area of the base (a square) is:\n\\[ \\text{Base area} = 12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\nSo, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:\nThe base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm, and its height is 4 cm. The area of the base (a square) is:\n\\[ \\text{Base area} = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\nSo, the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is:\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
